title: Unmounted volumes in the GUI
tags: [[Mount points]]
kind: reference
summary: Records behind an unplugged volume are shown in amber with the volume to plug back in — distinct from orphans, never offered for cleanup.

While a volume is unplugged its metarecords are still listed and queryable, but the
files are ''unavailable'', not deleted. The panels make the difference visible, since the
two look identical otherwise: an orphan is gone for good, an unavailable record comes
back with the drive.

The source is `GET /repos/:repo/mounts` ([[Mount status]]), re-read whenever a panel
reloads what it shows (a listing, a query, a repository switch). A daemon that cannot
answer degrades to "no mount points": a lost distinction, never a blocked display. A path
is unavailable at or below an `offline` mount point.

One vocabulary: the warning amber (never the error red, never the orphan purple) and one
sentence naming what to plug back in — `volume not mounted: label:PHOTOS
(/media/photos)`.

* ''metarecord-detail'' — an amber line above the fields when every path of the record is behind an offline mount point, checked before the orphan line and replacing it: a stale path on an unplugged drive is not an orphan.
* ''file'' — no preview is attempted; the sentence stands where "no preview available" would.
* ''file-manager'' — a banner above a listing at or below an offline mount point, and an `⏏ not mounted` badge (amber name, the sentence as tooltip) on such entries.
* ''metarecord-list'' — unavailable rows in amber with the sentence as tooltip; nothing is filtered out, browsing that metadata with the drive unplugged being the point.

Nothing offers to "clean up" unavailable records: orphan detection refuses them by design.
The helper is `panel-shim/mounts.js`.
